@baseUrl = http://localhost:4201
@apiVersion = 1
@domain = atlas
@workflow = money-transfer

### NOTE
# The .csx mappings carry "<base64; VS Code populates>" placeholders in their
# mapping.code fields. They satisfy schema validation, but the workflow will only
# execute at runtime once the vNext VS Code extension has opened & saved each
# component once (it base64-encodes the .csx into mapping.code). Do this before
# exercising the calls below.

# ============================================================================
# PATH A — FIRST transfer to an IBAN -> mobile push approval step
#   enter-transfer-details --submit-details--> review-and-confirm
#   --confirm (get-iban-history => isFirstTransfer=true)--> evaluate-push-requirement
#   --require-push (auto)--> awaiting-push-approval
#   --approve-push (manual)--> executing-transfer
#   --execution-succeeded (auto)--> transfer-completed
# ============================================================================

### 1. Start an instance (lands on Initial state enter-transfer-details)
# @name start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/start
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Capture the instance key from the start response
@instanceKey = {{start.response.body.$.id}}

### 2. Source-accounts LOV (sourceAccountId dropdown) — optional pre-fetch
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/functions/get-source-accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3. Favorite-beneficiaries LOV (favorite cards in the input view)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/functions/get-favorite-beneficiaries
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4. submit-details (enter-transfer-details -> review-and-confirm)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/transitions/submit-details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-1001",
  "targetIban": "TR120006200000000009999999",
  "amount": 2500.75,
  "currency": "TRY",
  "saveBeneficiary": false
}

### 5. confirm (review-and-confirm -> evaluate-push-requirement; runs get-iban-history)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/transitions/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6. Poll state — for a NEW iban, require-push auto-fires -> awaiting-push-approval
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/functions/state

### 7. approve-push (awaiting-push-approval -> executing-transfer)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/transitions/approve-push
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 8. Poll state — execution-succeeded auto-fires -> transfer-completed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/functions/state

# ============================================================================
# PATH B — KNOWN IBAN -> push step is skipped (skip-push auto transition)
#   ...--confirm (get-iban-history => isFirstTransfer=false)--> evaluate-push-requirement
#   --skip-push (auto)--> executing-transfer --execution-succeeded--> transfer-completed
# (Run PATH A first against the same targetIban so history exists.)
# ============================================================================

### B1. Start
# @name startKnown
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/start
Content-Type: application/json

{}

@knownKey = {{startKnown.response.body.$.id}}

### B2. submit-details (same targetIban as PATH A)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{knownKey}}/transitions/submit-details
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "ACC-1001",
  "targetIban": "TR120006200000000009999999",
  "amount": 100,
  "currency": "TRY"
}

### B3. confirm -> evaluate-push-requirement (skip-push expected)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{knownKey}}/transitions/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### B4. Poll state — should land directly on transfer-completed (no push)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{knownKey}}/functions/state

# ============================================================================
# PATH C — push timeout (PT5M) -> transfer-failed
#   At awaiting-push-approval, do NOT approve; after 5 minutes the push-timeout
#   timer fires -> transfer-failed. Poll state after the window to observe.
# ============================================================================

### C. Cancel from review-and-confirm -> transfer-cancelled (cancel transition)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceKey}}/transitions/cancel-transfer
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Query instances by state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances?state=transfer-completed
